0\"><li><a class=\"transition hover:text-red-600\" href=\"/\">Thumbnail Downloader</a></li><li><a class=\"transition hover:text-red-600\" href=\"/youtube-transcript\">Transcript Generator</a></li></ul></nav></div></header><div class=\"flex-1\"><main class=\"min-h-screen bg-slate-100\"><section class=\"mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-10 md:py-14\"><div class=\"text-center\"><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-3 hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity\" href=\"https://youtubethumbnails-downloader.com/\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-red-600 text-xl font-black text-white shadow-sm\">▶</div><span class=\"text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 md:text-2xl\">YouTube Thumbnail Downloader</span></a></div><div class=\"mt-10 text-center\"><h1 class=\"text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 md:text-6xl\">YouTube Thumbnail Downloader: HD &amp; Max Resolution, Free</h1><p class=\"mx-auto mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600\">Paste a YouTube link into the<!-- --> <a class=\"text-red-600 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-red-700\" href=\"https://youtubethumbnails-downloader.com/\">YouTube Thumbnail Downloader</a> <!-- -->and you get every thumbnail size that video has: Max Resolution (1280×720), SD, HQ, MQ and the tiny default, each labeled with its real pixel size. It handles YouTube Shorts too, and links from Vimeo, TikTok, Dailymotion, Facebook, X/Twitter and Bilibili. Free, no sign-up, no watermark, nothing to install.</p></div><div class=\"mx-auto mt-16 flex justify-center\"><div class=\"w-full max-w-2xl\"><form class=\"w-full max-w-3xl rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-lg\"><div class=\"relative\"><input type=\"text\" inputMode=\"url\" autoComplete=\"off\" autoCorrect=\"off\" spellCheck=\"false\" placeholder=\"Paste video URL here...\" aria-label=\"Paste video URL\" class=\"w-full rounded-xl border border-gray-300 bg-white py-4 pl-5 pr-28 text-base text-gray-900 placeholder:text-gray-400 outline-none transition focus:border-black disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:bg-gray-100 sm:pr-36 sm:text-lg\" value=\"\"/><button type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Paste video URL from clipboard\" class=\"absolute right-2 top-1/2 flex -translate-y-1/2 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg bg-black px-3 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-gray-800 active:scale-95 disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:bg-gray-700 sm:px-4 sm:text-sm\">📋 Paste Link</button></div><button type=\"submit\" aria-label=\"Get thumbnail\" class=\"mt-5 flex w-full items-center justify-center gap-3 rounded-xl bg-black py-4 text-lg font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-gray-800 active:scale-95 disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:bg-gray-700\">Get Thumbnail</button></form></div></div><section class=\"mx-auto mt-12 max-w-4xl\"><a class=\"flex items-center justify-between gap-6 rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:shadow-md md:p-8\" href=\"/youtube-transcript\"><div><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-red-600\">Free tool</p><h2 class=\"mt-1 text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 md:text-2xl\">YouTube Transcript Generator</h2><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">Need the words instead of the picture? Paste a YouTube link and get the video&#x27;s transcript as text, with optional timestamps.</p></div><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-3xl text-red-600\">→</span></a></section><nav aria-label=\"On this page\" class=\"mx-auto mt-16 max-w-4xl rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm md:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900\">On this page</h2><ul class=\"mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm font-medium\"><li><a href=\"#download-youtube-thumbnail\" class=\"text-red-600 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-red-700\">Download in HD</a></li><li><a href=\"#youtube-thumbnail-sizes\" class=\"text-red-600 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-red-700\">Thumbnail sizes</a></li><li><a href=\"#youtube-thumbnail-url\" class=\"text-red-600 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-red-700\">Thumbnail URL format</a></li><li><a href=\"#youtube-shorts-thumbnail\" class=\"text-red-600 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-red-700\">Shorts thumbnails</a></li><li><a href=\"#supported-platforms\" class=\"text-red-600 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-red-700\">Other platforms</a></li><li><a href=\"#faq\" class=\"text-red-600 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-red-700\">FAQ</a></li></ul></nav><section class=\"mx-auto mt-20 max-w-4xl rounded-2xl bg-white p-8 shadow-sm md:p-10\"><div class=\"space-y-6 leading-8 text-gray-600\"><p><strong class=\"text-gray-900\">No broken image links:</strong> <!-- -->A lot of thumbnail grabbers just build a maxresdefault.jpg URL and hand it over, even when that file doesn&#x27;t exist. Our<!-- --> <a class=\"text-red-600 font-medium underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-red-700\" href=\"https://youtubethumbnails-downloader.com/\">online YouTube thumbnail downloader</a> <!-- -->tests maxresdefault, sddefault, hqdefault, mqdefault and default against the actual video and lists only the ones that load.</p><p><strong class=\"text-gray-900\">Pixel size on every card:</strong> <!-- -->Each result shows its real width and height, so you know whether you&#x27;re getting a 1280×720 HD thumbnail or a 480×360 one before you click. Handy when you&#x27;re picking an image for a redesign, a blog post, a slide, or a competitor comparison.</p><p><strong class=\"text-gray-900\">One box, seven platforms:</strong> <!-- -->Paste a link from YouTube, YouTube Shorts, Vimeo, TikTok, Dailymotion, Facebook, X/Twitter or Bilibili. The site is detected from the URL, so there&#x27;s no menu to pick from and no second tool to open.</p></div></section><section id=\"download-youtube-thumbnail\" class=\"mt-20 scroll-mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-white p-8 shadow-sm md:p-10\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900\">How to Download a YouTube Thumbnail in HD (1280×720)</h2><p class=\"mt-4 leading-8 text-gray-600\">Every video you upload to YouTube gets a set of preview images generated automatically. They&#x27;re what people see in search results, on the home feed, in suggested videos, in playlists and on channel pages. Since the thumbnail is often the first thing a viewer notices, plenty of people want the original file: to see how a competitor lays theirs out, to rebuild one of their own in an editor, to keep a record of past designs, or to use a cover image in a blog post.</p><p class=\"mt-4 leading-8 text-gray-600\">You could dig through the page source or guess the image URL by hand, but it&#x27;s slow and often ends in a broken link. Here you paste the video link, the tool checks which sizes YouTube really stored for that upload, and you download the one you need as a JPG.</p><h3 class=\"mt-10 text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900\">Download a YouTube Thumbnail in 3 Steps</h3><ol class=\"mt-4 list-decimal space-y-3 pl-6 leading-7 text-gray-600\"><li><strong class=\"text-gray-900\">Copy the video link.</strong> <!-- -->A normal watch URL, a youtu.be short link or a Shorts URL all work.</li><li><strong class=\"text-gray-900\">Paste it into<!-- --> <a class=\"text-red-600 underline hover:text-red-700\" href=\"https://youtubethumbnails-downloader.com/\">youtubethumbnails-downloader.com</a>.</strong> <!-- -->The platform and video ID are picked up automatically.</li><li><strong class=\"text-gray-900\">Choose a size and download.</strong> <!-- -->Compare the cards by pixel size and save the one you want, or grab everything in one ZIP.</li></ol><h3 class=\"mt-10 text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900\">Which YouTube Links Does It Accept?</h3><p class=\"mt-4 leading-8 text-gray-600\">Regular youtube.com/watch?v= links, shortened youtu.be links, embed URLs and youtube.com/shorts/ links all work. The tool pulls the video ID out of whichever one you paste, so you don&#x27;t need to trim tracking parameters or clean the URL first.</p><h3 id=\"youtube-thumbnail-sizes\" class=\"mt-10 scroll-mt-6 text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900\">YouTube Thumbnail Sizes and Resolutions</h3><p class=\"mt-4 leading-8 text-gray-600\">YouTube keeps several sizes of each thumbnail under fixed file names. This tool checks every one of them:</p><div class=\"mt-4 overflow-x-auto\"><table class=\"w-full min-w-[640px] border-collapse text-left text-sm\"><thead><tr class=\"border-b border-gray-200\"><th class=\"px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900\">Label</th><th class=\"px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900\">Typical dimensions</th><th class=\"px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900\">Best for</th></tr></thead><tbody class=\"text-gray-600\"><tr class=\"border-b border-gray-100\"><td class=\"px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900\">Max Resolution</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3\">1280 × 720 (when available)</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3\">Redesigns, print, close-up study</td></tr><tr class=\"border-b border-gray-100\"><td class=\"px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900\">SD</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3\">640 × 480</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3\">Blog covers, mid-size previews</td></tr><tr class=\"border-b border-gray-100\"><td class=\"px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900\">HQ</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3\">480 × 360</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3\">Safe fallback, most videos have it</td></tr><tr class=\"border-b border-gray-100\"><td class=\"px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900\">MQ</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3\">320 × 180</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3\">Small embeds and lists</td></tr><tr><td class=\"px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900\">Default</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3\">120 × 90</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3\">Tiny previews and icons</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"mt-5 leading-8 text-gray-600\">Max Resolution isn&#x27;t there for every video. YouTube only makes it when the original upload was good enough. If you don&#x27;t see that card, HQ (480×360) is the one most likely to exist.</p><h3 class=\"mt-10 text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900\">What Makes a YouTube Thumbnail Get Clicked</h3><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 leading-7 text-gray-600\"><p><strong class=\"text-gray-900\">1. One thing to look at.</strong> <!-- -->A face, a product or a single clear scene reads at thumbnail size. A crowded frame doesn&#x27;t.</p><p><strong class=\"text-gray-900\">2. Decide what&#x27;s seen first.</strong> <!-- -->Size, brightness and position tell the eye where to go, so use them on purpose.</p><p><strong class=\"text-gray-900\">3. Fewer words, bigger.</strong> <!-- -->Two or three words survive on a phone screen. A sentence doesn&#x27;t.</p><p><strong class=\"text-gray-900\">4. Contrast, but not everywhere.</strong> <!-- -->Make the subject and text stand apart from the background instead of cranking saturation on everything.</p><p><strong class=\"text-gray-900\">5. Check it small.</strong> <!-- -->Shrink your draft to phone size before you publish. If you can&#x27;t read it, viewers won&#x27;t either.</p><p><strong class=\"text-gray-900\">6. Keep the promise.</strong> <!-- -->Curiosity gets the click, but a thumbnail that misleads costs you watch time and trust.</p><p><strong class=\"text-gray-900\">7. Cut the decoration.</strong> <!-- -->If an element doesn&#x27;t help the main message, it&#x27;s getting in its way.</p><p><strong class=\"text-gray-900\">8. Study the pattern, not the pixels.</strong> <!-- -->Download competitor thumbnails at full size, look at their layout and colors, then make something of your own.</p></div><h3 id=\"youtube-thumbnail-url\" class=\"mt-10 scroll-mt-6 text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900\">YouTube Thumbnail URL Format (img.youtube.com)</h3><p class=\"mt-4 leading-8 text-gray-600\">Every YouTube thumbnail lives at an address built from the video ID. Swap VIDEO_ID for the ID of your video (the part after v= in a watch link):</p><ul class=\"mt-4 space-y-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\"><li><code class=\"rounded bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 text-sm text-gray-900\">https://img.youtube.com/vi/VIDEO_ID/maxresdefault.jpg</code> <!-- -->for 1280 × 720</li><li><code class=\"rounded bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 text-sm text-gray-900\">https://img.youtube.com/vi/VIDEO_ID/sddefault.jpg</code> <!-- -->for 640 × 480</li><li><code class=\"rounded bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 text-sm text-gray-900\">https://img.youtube.com/vi/VIDEO_ID/hqdefault.jpg</code> <!-- -->for 480 × 360</li><li><code class=\"rounded bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 text-sm text-gray-900\">https://img.youtube.com/vi/VIDEO_ID/mqdefault.jpg</code> <!-- -->for 320 × 180</li><li><code class=\"rounded bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 text-sm text-gray-900\">https://img.youtube.com/vi/VIDEO_ID/default.jpg</code> <!-- -->for 120 × 90</li></ul><p class=\"mt-4 leading-8 text-gray-600\">If a maxresdefault address shows a broken image, that video has no 1280×720 file. Pasting the link above saves you from testing each address by hand.</p><h3 id=\"youtube-shorts-thumbnail\" class=\"mt-10 scroll-mt-6 text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900\">Download a YouTube Shorts Thumbnail</h3><p class=\"mt-4 leading-8 text-gray-600\">Shorts use the same video-ID system as regular uploads, so a youtube.com/shorts/ link behaves like a watch link here. Paste it, look at the image sizes YouTube generated for that Short, and download the one you need for cross-posting or your portfolio.</p><h3 class=\"mt-10 text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900\">Works on Phone and Desktop, No Extension Needed</h3><p class=\"mt-4 leading-8 text-gray-600\">It all happens in your browser tab, whether that&#x27;s a laptop, an Android phone, an iPhone or a tablet. No app, no browser extension, no account. Paste, check, download.</p><h3 class=\"mt-10 text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900\">If the Thumbnail Won&#x27;t Download</h3><p class=\"mt-4 leading-8 text-gray-600\">When nothing loads, first check that you pasted the whole URL and that the video is public. Private, deleted, age-restricted and region-blocked videos don&#x27;t return usable thumbnail data.</p><p class=\"mt-4 leading-8 text-gray-600\">If you only see a few sizes, that&#x27;s normal. Not every video has a Max Resolution file, so go with the biggest one the tool shows rather than expecting all five.</p><h3 class=\"mt-10 text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900\">Copyright and Fair Use</h3><p class=\"mt-4 leading-8 text-gray-600\">Anyone can see a thumbnail, but that doesn&#x27;t make it public domain. The channel or creator generally owns the artwork. Use this tool for previewing, research and comparison, and get permission before you republish someone else&#x27;s thumbnail or use it commercially.</p></section><section id=\"supported-platforms\" class=\"mt-16 scroll-mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-white p-8 shadow-sm md:p-10\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900\">Vimeo, TikTok, Dailymotion, Facebook, X/Twitter &amp; Bilibili Thumbnail Downloader</h2><p class=\"mt-4 leading-8 text-gray-600\">The same search box also recognises public Vimeo, TikTok, Dailymotion, Facebook, X/Twitter and Bilibili links. You don&#x27;t pick a platform first, and you don&#x27;t need a separate downloader for each site.</p><div class=\"mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2\"><article id=\"vimeo-thumbnail-downloader\" class=\"scroll-mt-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-6\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-gray-900\">Vimeo Thumbnail Downloader</h3><p class=\"mt-3 leading-7 text-gray-600\">Paste a public Vimeo link to get its cover image at the highest resolution available. Good for design research, presentations and tidying up a video library. To download a Vimeo thumbnail, copy the video&#x27;s page link, paste it above and save the cover image.</p></article><article id=\"tiktok-thumbnail-downloader\" class=\"scroll-mt-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-6\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-gray-900\">TikTok Thumbnail Downloader</h3><p class=\"mt-3 leading-7 text-gray-600\">Drop in a public TikTok video link, check the cover frame, then save it. Useful for cross-posting or planning content. To download a TikTok video thumbnail, copy the video link from the app or browser and paste it above.</p></article><article id=\"dailymotion-thumbnail-downloader\" class=\"scroll-mt-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-6\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-gray-900\">Dailymotion Thumbnail Downloader</h3><p class=\"mt-3 leading-7 text-gray-600\">A public Dailymotion link returns its preview image, which you can look over and download straight away. To download a Dailymotion thumbnail, paste the video&#x27;s page URL above.</p></article><article id=\"facebook-video-thumbnail-downloader\" class=\"scroll-mt-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-6\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-gray-900\">Facebook Video Thumbnail Downloader</h3><p class=\"mt-3 leading-7 text-gray-600\">Works on public Facebook videos that expose thumbnail metadata. Private or restricted posts won&#x27;t return anything. To download a Facebook video thumbnail, copy the link of the public video and paste it above.</p></article><article id=\"x-twitter-video-thumbnail-downloader\" class=\"scroll-mt-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-6\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-gray-900\">X/Twitter Video Thumbnail Downloader</h3><p class=\"mt-3 leading-7 text-gray-600\">Paste the URL of a public X/Twitter post with a video in it and the preview image comes back, the same way a YouTube link would. To download a Twitter or X video thumbnail, copy the post link and paste it above.</p></article><article id=\"bilibili-thumbnail-downloader\" class=\"scroll-mt-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-6\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-gray-900\">Bilibili Thumbnail Downloader</h3><p class=\"mt-3 leading-7 text-gray-600\">Public Bilibili links and supported short URLs return their cover image so you can preview and download it. To download a Bilibili thumbnail, paste the video link or a supported short URL above.</p></article></div><h3 class=\"mt-10 text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900\">How the Platform Gets Detected</h3><ol class=\"mt-4 list-decimal space-y-3 pl-6 leading-7 text-gray-600\"><li>Copy a public video or post link from any supported site.</li><li>Paste it into the search box at the top of the page.</li><li>The platform is worked out from the URL.</li><li>The available thumbnail data is fetched for that link.</li><li>Check the image and its dimensions.</li><li>Download the version you need, or all of them as a ZIP.</li></ol><p class=\"mt-6 leading-8 text-gray-600\">Each site exposes a different number of sizes, so results won&#x27;t be identical everywhere. The tool shows what it can actually retrieve for your link and doesn&#x27;t pretend otherwise.</p></section><section class=\"mt-16 rounded-2xl bg-white p-8 shadow-sm md:p-10\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900\">Why People Use This Thumbnail Grabber</h2><p class=\"mt-4 leading-8 text-gray-600\">Getting a thumbnail used to mean right-click saving a blurry preview, or typing out an img.youtube.com address and hoping it worked. With<!-- --> <a class=\"text-red-600 underline hover:text-red-700\" href=\"https://youtubethumbnails-downloader.com/\">youtubethumbnails-downloader.com</a> <!-- -->you paste a link and see every size that really exists, with its actual dimensions, so you pick the right file on the first try.</p><p class=\"mt-4 leading-8 text-gray-600\">There&#x27;s one rule behind it: show only what can be retrieved for that specific video. No placeholders, and no broken links passed off as working thumbnails.</p><p class=\"mt-4 leading-8 text-gray-600\">People use it for thumbnail redesign research, competitor benchmarking, portfolio archives, blog and course covers, classroom projects and reference images for editing. Within whatever the rights holder allows, of course.</p></section><section id=\"faq\" class=\"mt-16 scroll-mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-white p-8 shadow-sm md:p-10\"><h2 class=\"text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900\">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class=\"mt-8 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2\"><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">What is a YouTube thumbnail downloader?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">It&#x27;s a free online tool that takes a public video link and returns every thumbnail image YouTube has stored for it, including the 1280×720 max resolution version. You can look at each size, compare them, and save the one you want. No screenshots, no YouTube Studio.</p></article><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">How do I download a YouTube thumbnail in HD?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">Paste the video link into the box at the top and wait a second for the results. If a Max Resolution (1280×720) card shows up, hit Download on it. If it doesn&#x27;t, the video has no HD thumbnail file, and the next biggest card in the list (SD or HQ) is the best you can get.</p></article><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">How do I download a YouTube thumbnail in full size, 1280x720?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">Look for the Max Resolution card. That&#x27;s the 1280×720 file, also known as maxresdefault. Some videos don&#x27;t have it, usually older or lower-quality uploads, so if the card is missing, the video simply doesn&#x27;t have a 1280×720 thumbnail on YouTube&#x27;s servers.</p></article><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">Can I download a thumbnail from a YouTube Shorts link?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">Yes. Paste a youtube.com/shorts/ link exactly as you would a normal watch link. The tool reads the video ID from it and returns whatever thumbnail sizes exist for that Short.</p></article><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">What size should a YouTube thumbnail be?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">1280 × 720 pixels, 16:9, saved as JPG, GIF, or PNG and under 2MB. That&#x27;s the size YouTube asks for. Leave enough room around the subject, because the image gets shrunk a lot in search results and suggested videos.</p></article><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">What&#x27;s the difference between maxresdefault, sddefault, hqdefault, mqdefault, and default?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">They&#x27;re the file names YouTube uses for each size: maxresdefault is 1280×720 (not on every video), sddefault is 640×480, hqdefault is 480×360, mqdefault is 320×180, and default is 120×90. This tool checks each one against your video and only lists the ones that actually load.</p></article><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">Why is the Max Resolution thumbnail missing for some videos?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">YouTube doesn&#x27;t create a 1280×720 thumbnail for every upload. It tends to be missing on older videos or ones uploaded at low quality. When that happens, HQ (480×360) is the safest fallback, since almost every video has it.</p></article><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">How do I save a YouTube thumbnail on my iPhone or Android phone?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">Open this page in your phone&#x27;s browser, paste the video link, and tap Download on the size you want. Nothing to install. It works the same way on iPhone, Android, tablets, and desktop.</p></article><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">Is this YouTube thumbnail downloader free? Do I need to sign up?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">It&#x27;s free. No account, no login, no watermark on the images. Paste a link, look at the results, download.</p></article><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">Can I also download thumbnails from Vimeo, TikTok, Dailymotion, Facebook, X/Twitter, and Bilibili?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">Yes. The same search box recognises public links from those sites and fetches whatever thumbnail they expose. How many sizes you get depends on the platform.</p></article><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">Can I download all the thumbnail sizes at once?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">Yes. If a video returns more than one size, a Download All Thumbnails button appears above the results and packs every available image into one ZIP file.</p></article><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">How do I get the thumbnail image URL of a YouTube video?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">YouTube thumbnails sit at img.youtube.com/vi/VIDEO_ID/maxresdefault.jpg, with VIDEO_ID swapped for the ID of your video. You can type that out yourself, but if the video has no maxresdefault file you&#x27;ll get a broken image. This tool checks which files exist so you don&#x27;t have to guess.</p></article><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">Can I reuse a downloaded thumbnail in my own video or commercially?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">Not without permission. A thumbnail being visible to everyone doesn&#x27;t make it free to use. The creator usually owns the artwork, so ask before putting it in your own video, an ad, or anything you sell.</p></article><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">Can I download a thumbnail from a private YouTube video?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">No. Private, deleted, age-restricted and region-blocked videos don&#x27;t return usable thumbnail data, so the tool has nothing to fetch. The video needs to be public.</p></article><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">What file format do the downloaded thumbnails come in?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">The images in the ZIP from Download All Thumbnails are saved as JPG files, named after their size so they&#x27;re easy to tell apart.</p></article><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">How do I download a TikTok video thumbnail?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">Copy the link of a public TikTok video, paste it into the search box at the top, and the cover image loads for you to preview and save.</p></article><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">How do I download a Facebook video thumbnail?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">Paste the link of a public Facebook video into the search box. If the post is private or restricted, Facebook doesn&#x27;t expose a thumbnail, so nothing will come back.</p></article><article><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold leading-7 text-gray-900\">Why would I need to download my own YouTube thumbnail?</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-600\">Mostly for housekeeping: saving old thumbnails for a portfolio, putting an old design next to a new one for an A/B comparison, or reusing a Shorts cover on another platform. Plenty of people also use it to look at a competitor&#x27;s thumbnail at full size for research.</p></article></div></section></section></main><script id=\"faq-schema\" type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is a YouTube thumbnail downloader?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"It's a free online tool that takes a public video link and returns every thumbnail image YouTube has stored for it, including the 1280×720 max resolution version. You can look at each size, compare them, and save the one you want. No screenshots, no YouTube Studio.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How do I download a YouTube thumbnail in HD?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Paste the video link into the box at the top and wait a second for the results. If a Max Resolution (1280×720) card shows up, hit Download on it. If it doesn't, the video has no HD thumbnail file, and the next biggest card in the list (SD or HQ) is the best you can get.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How